            <ArticleTitle>Severe back pain following epidural analgesia in patients with spinocerebellar ataxia: a report of two cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>314-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jclinane.2010.07.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two patients with spinocerebellar ataxia received epidural analgesia with no exacerbation of their symptoms. The patients developed transient, but extremely severe, low back pain as a result of the epidural analgesia.</AbstractText>
